1
00:00:01,753 --> 00:00:05,335
Meet Literate: a free, open-source reader
for articles,

2
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:08,530
selected text, and local PDFs.

3
00:00:08,530 --> 00:00:11,270
In Settings, choose Instant for the
quickest start with

4
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:14,795
installed device voices. Or choose Natural
for Kokoro,

5
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:17,055
which downloads its model before first
use.

6
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:19,935
Open an article, click Literate, and press
Play.

7
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:22,995
Follow the highlighted words. For a
shorter passage,

8
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:26,295
select the text, right-click, and choose
Read selection aloud.

9
00:00:26,590 --> 00:00:30,250
Want to skip a sidebar? Choose section,
point at the part you want,

10
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:33,115
and click. Literate reads that section.

11
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:35,895
Open the mini-player to follow the
scrolling words.

12
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:40,095
Click a word to jump there. Use the pin to
keep the player above other windows.

13
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:44,795
Adjust the speed, switch between light and
dark, and choose your accent color.

14
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:50,355
For local PDFs, enable Allow access to
file URLs in Chrome’s extension settings.

15
00:00:50,730 --> 00:00:55,315
Then open the PDF. Scanned documents need
text recognition first.

16
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:57,650
Your reading stays on your device.

17
00:00:57,650 --> 00:01:01,535
Keep the original page open, find your
pace, and listen.
